"Serialize CSSUnparsedValue directly in toString" (crbugs 577378379 and
580175468, not public; no CVE listed yet): CSSUnparsedValue.toString() went
through ToCSSValue() and the CSS parser, which depend on main-thread-only
data, also when called off the main thread (worklets). The fix serializes
the segments directly and checks that declaration parsing stays on the main
thread. chromium/src main commit 7c84d3eadb2cb9e089e16b0382079700aa2ebc77
(2026-10-30), merged on 2026-11-02 to 157
(d054e379217278be788e03921f4bb27306cbf66a, after the 157.0.8103.37 tag).
This is the 157 merge, without its tests. Drop it once a 157 tag has it.

